      "body": "# [AMD] DSA: allow breakable prefill CUDA graph on HIP\r\n\r\n## What\r\nTwo CUDA-only checks in the DSA prefill graph path now also accept HIP:\r\n- `pcg_dsa_indexer_prefill_split`: `assert _is_cuda` -> `assert _is_cuda or _is_hip`\r\n- `is_dsa_prefill_cp_interleave`: `is_cuda()` -> `(is_cuda() or is_hip())`\r\n\r\nThis makes `--cuda-graph-backend-prefill breakable` usable for DSA models\r\n(GLM-5.2, DeepSeek-V3.2) on ROCm. The default backend is unchanged.\r\n\r\n## Why\r\nEager prefill on MI355X is launch-bound for short and medium prompts. The DSA\r\nindexer split already works under HIP graphs; only the platform guards blocked it.\r\n\r\n## E2E\r\nMI355X TP4, GLM-5.2-MXFP4, EAGLE MTP (3 steps, 4 draft tokens), OSL 1024,\r\nmax running 48, `--cuda-graph-backend-prefill breakable` vs eager prefill.\r\n\r\n| ISL | conc | TTFT ms | TPOT ms |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| 1024 | 4 | 138 -> 102 (-26%) | 4.22 -> 4.08 (-3.3%) |\r\n| 1024 | 64 | 3247 -> 3194 (-2%) | 13.18 -> 13.09 (-0.7%) |\r\n| 8192 | 4 | 340 -> 346 (+2%) | 4.85 -> 4.88 (+0.7%) |\r\n| 8192 | 64 | 7040 -> 7088 (+1%) | 24.38 -> 24.74 (+1.5%) |\r\n\r\nGeomean over these 4 points: TTFT -7.3%, TPOT -0.5%, throughput flat.\r\nFull 10-point sweep together with the non-fused decode AR change: TTFT -12% to -27%\r\nat 1k c4..c32 and -27% at 8k c16; c64 TTFT is queueing-dominated and unchanged.\r\ngsm8k unchanged (0.93).\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\n- No change on CUDA. On HIP the feature stays opt-in.\r\n\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38496928815](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38496928815)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38496928739](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38496928739)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38496928713](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38496928713)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
